    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Oppenheimer and Volkoff&#x27;s 1939 relativistic generalization of hydrostatic equilibrium predicts something Newtonian gravity cannot: a maximum possible mass for a neutron star. The star&#x27;s matter is modeled as a polytrope, P = K\rho_0^\Gamma, relating pressure to rest-mass density, with total energy density (rest mass plus internal energy) \varepsilon = \rho_0 + P/(\Gamma-1). Enclosed mass m(r) and pressure P(r) then obey the Tolman-Oppenheimer-Volkoff equations">

